<!--BlockML Documentation — render A04 pages in place (semantic scaffold → real content)
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.task.A04_02_RenderPages-->
<task:A04_02_RenderPages xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:source="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source"
  xmlns:lrule="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.rule"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that renders A04 pages in place from semantic scaffold to real content
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A04 rendering task: rewrite each imported A04 DocPage in BML so semantic
    scaffold becomes reader-facing content — not an export to HTML, JSON, or
    another format.

    - **Import** — A04_01_CopyData already wiped A04 data and imported the
      full A03 data tree with packages and names remapped
    - **Input** — live A04 DocSet and pages (purpose, message, roles, scopes,
      sources, supportingPoints, and the content tree)
    - **Output** — the same A04 page Files, with real body slots filled and
      semantic / claim metadata removed; do not redesign structure or invent
      pages absent from BmlDocSet_A04
    - **Style** — CompleteSentenceRule and CodeStyleRule apply here
    - **Sources** — authorativeSources is BlockMLSourceSet; page- and
      element-level sets on the imported pages are the content ceiling while
      rendering, then are stripped from the written pages
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          Render every A04 page in place: turn the imported semantic scaffold
          into finished reader-facing BML content on the same DocPages. Do not
          export to HTML, JSON, Markdown, or any other manifestation. Do not
          redesign DocPage.content structure, invent pages, or edit A01 / A02 /
          A03 BML.

          A04_01_CopyData has already wiped live A04 data and imported the
          full A03 data tree with packages and names remapped. This task does
          not copy or delete A04 data. Do not invent pages that are not in
          BmlDocSet_A04.pages. Do not edit A03.

          1. Read the imported A04 pages (specification)
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.data.BmlDocSet_A04.
          Walk BmlDocSet_A04.pages in listed order. For each DocPage, inspect
          title, purpose, detailLevel, pageType, page-level
          authoritativeSources / scopes / readerOutcomes /
          learningObjectives / exclusions / supportingPoints / audiences, and
          the content tree (Section, Paragraph, List, ListItem, CodeBlock,
          Image, Navigation, and their message / role / weight / detailLevel /
          element semantics / authoritativeSources).

          Those fields are the specification for this render. Do not invent
          claims outside page and element scopes. Do not dump sources.
          Element authoritativeSources remain subsets of the page set while
          reading.

          2. Open authoritative sources
          Resolve this task's authorativeSources TypeSelectors (scan type
          for each selector on org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source.BlockMLSourceSet).
          For each Block named by a page or element source set, inspect
          is, documentation, and references before writing prose or code.
          Domain claims in the rendered body may come only from those bound
          Blocks (and A04 pages for Navigation targets).

          Never link a Block from another sector (a01, a02, a03, or any
          later sector). Never keep an A03 page or PageGroup FQN on an
          A04 page.

          3. Fill real content slots (same tree)
          Follow DocPage.content order. Keep Section nesting, List/ListItem
          structure, Navigation items, and element order. Do not independently
          add, remove, or reorder Sections to satisfy taste. If the scaffold
          is insufficient, report the gap; do not silently redesign A04 data
          or edit A03.

          Derive finished content from purpose, message, role, detailLevel,
          weight, supportingPoints, exclusions, scopes, outcomes, and
          authoritativeSources, then write it into the real body slots:

          - Section — keep or generate heading (type:Text); leave content
            children in place
          - Paragraph — fill content with one or more page:Text runs whose
            text property holds the finished prose (complete sentences).
            Prefer one primary idea per paragraph (OnePrimaryMessageRule)
          - page:Text — set text to the literal character content
          - CodeBlock — set code to the complete listing (CodeExampleRule);
            after every listing, the following explanatory element must
            already exist in the tree or be the next scaffolded element
            (CodeExplanationRule) — do not invent a new Section for it
          - List — keep items; do not rely on List.message as body
          - ListItem — set text to the finished item lead; nest further
            BlockElements in content only when the scaffold already has them
          - Image — keep or fill src; set alt from message / purpose /
            sources when alt is missing
          - Navigation / NavigationItem — keep title, label, summary, target;
            target may name only A04 pages listed on BmlDocSet_A04; do not
            invent conceptual body on index / menu pages

          Apply while writing:
          - Respect Scope and Exclusion as hard bounds
          - Match DetailLevel: omit internal FQNs, diagnostics, and
            implementation notes at Introductory / Overview levels
          - Prefer concept before implementation in the rendered flow
          - Fill section depth so the subject is understandable
            (SectionCompletenessRule) without filler or repetition
            (AvoidContentRepetitionRule)
          - Use vocabulary appropriate to the declared Audience when
            audiences are set (AudienceVocabularyRule)
          - Prose uses complete sentences (CompleteSentenceRule)
          - Code presentation intent: preformatted, highlighted, read-only,
            with copy control (CodeStyleRule) — express that in the filled
            code / surrounding prose, not by exporting another format

          4. Strip semantic and claim metadata
          After body slots are filled, remove specification altitude from
          each written A04 page so the page carries real content only:

          On DocPage: remove authoritativeSources, scopes, readerOutcomes,
          learningObjectives, exclusions, supportingPoints, audiences, and
          purpose. Keep title, docset, pageType, detailLevel, rules (if any),
          and the content tree.

          On every Section, Navigation, NavigationItem, and page:Text: remove
          purpose once heading / labels / text are filled.

          On every ContentElement (Paragraph, List, ListItem, CodeBlock,
          Image): remove message, role, weight, detailLevel,
          authoritativeSources, audiences, supportingPoints, readerOutcomes,
          learningObjectives, scopes, exclusions, and purpose. Keep the real
          body slots (Paragraph.content, CodeBlock.code, ListItem.text,
          Image.src / alt, List.items, nested content).

          Do not leave empty semantic aggregations. Do not reintroduce A03
          package names. Do not remove A03 catalog entries.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
  <aggregations>
    <rules override="true">
      <composition>
        <lrule:RespectScopeRule />
        <lrule:RespectExclusionsRule />
        <lrule:MatchDetailLevelRule />
        <lrule:ConceptBeforeImplementationRule />
        <lrule:NoSourceDumpRule />
        <lrule:NoUnrequestedDiagnosticsRule />
        <lrule:OnePrimaryMessageRule />
        <lrule:SectionCompletenessRule />
        <lrule:AvoidContentRepetitionRule />
        <lrule:CodeExampleRule />
        <lrule:CodeExplanationRule />
        <lrule:AudienceVocabularyRule />
        <lrule:CompleteSentenceRule />
        <lrule:CodeStyleRule />
      </composition>
    </rules>
    <authorativeSources override="true">
      <composition>
        <source:BlockMLSourceSet />
      </composition>
    </authorativeSources>
  </aggregations>
</task:A04_02_RenderPages>
